readout=the additive rim is a +22,+20,+22 word in owner space, while
the multiplicative fold is the two-adic map u=2t mod1 used by the
phase pullback.  In this row, n+2-style rim data names the seam owners;
n*2-style folding names the branch sheet on which the phase flow bypasses
the seam.

## Bold Reframes
1. Forbidden-seam theorem target:
   If a max-delta mirror seam has zero compatible q=14V phase hits and
   its complement has mirror-balanced lower-delta same-component hits,
   then the seam is a boundary-gluing clause, not a wall obstruction.
2. Punctured-cylinder theorem target:
   A hard/currentless row with four mirror-paired dead islands, connected
   rescue graph, and a seven-owner seam should discharge by proving that
   every attempted seam saturation cuts off one of the 94 low-rank escapes
   or violates the phase-branch mirror flow.
3. Experiment design:
   Build a seam-complement graph whose vertices are survivor gates minus
   the hard seam.  Send the 282 phase witnesses through it and test whether
   every connected phase-flow component reaches a low-rank escape before
   it can cross the forbidden seam.  Then repeat on all hard orbits and
   classify zero-hit seams versus genuine phase walls.

